  "description": [
   {
    "value": "Mark Twain was an American writer. He was born on November 30, 1835, in Florida, Missouri. He spent his childhood in the town of Hannibal on the Mississippi. He was apprenticed to a typesetter, and later published a newspaper with his brother in Hannibal, then in Mescatine and Keokuk, Iowa. In 1857, he became an apprentice pilot, fulfilling his childhood dream of \"knowing the river,\" and in April 1859, he received his pilot's license. In 1861, he moved to Nevada...",
    "lang": "en",
    "via": "llm-page:biography",
    "file": "P7433.json",
    "uri": false
   }
  ],
